Hi Virginia,

I actually don't think multiple group modelling is what you want here, because each groups should technically contain independent individuals (like male/female, university/graduate students, etc). You might want something more like this for longitudinal IRT models: http://philchalmers.github.io/mirt/html/Longitudinal-IRT.html. Admittedly this is more complicated than I'd like, and the example needs to be simplified using the more modern syntax. But unfortunately I haven't had the time to fix it, so hopefully you can make due in the meantime. Cheers.

Phil

